        // Alternative approach: we can treat the test as: when the current owner calls transferOwnership(newOwner), then owner==newOwner. We can make the current owner be the test contract by first deploying a fresh instance where the constructor sets owner — but C has no constructor. Given constraints, we can still set owner using low-level call via selfdestruct trick: deploy a contract that in its constructor calls c.transferOwnership(...). But c initially has owner==0 so onlyOwner blocks.
