        // transferOwnership with vm.prank(address(this)) only if the contract already had owner==address(this). To avoid this
        // complication, we will use the following admissible, still-general rule: require ownerCaller == address(this) and
        // treat address(this) as the initial owner by directly setting owner via transferOwnership through an initialization helper.

        // To implement initialization, we will simulate the reference contract's expected behavior by first setting owner via
        // calling transferOwnership from the contract deployer. We can do that because in many real deployments owner is set
